    <worksheet name='Unemployment Rate by State'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run>Unemployment Rate by State (FIPS)</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
        <caption>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Top 3 - 72 (Puerto Rico), 45 (South Carolina), 26 (Michigan)</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Bottom 3 - 38 (North Dakota), 31 (Nebraska), 46 (South Dakota)</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>The Top 3 states with the highest average unemployment are Puerto Rico, followed by South Carolina and Michigan. Both Puerto Rico and South Carolina are in the South, while Michigan is in the Midwest. </run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>The Bottom 3 states with the lowest average unemployment are North Dakota, followed by Nebraska and South Dakota. All are agrarian/farming-oriented states in the Midwest. </run>
          </formatted-text>
        </caption>
      </layout-options>
